			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2826967">
									

<p>You did an incredible job blending the surreality/body horror with the psychological/existential horror in a way where it doesn't feel overused or cliche. The events in the journal do a great job of describing the emotional experience involved without downplaying or exaggerating anything - it reads as if a genuine journal. The evaporation of the bodies after death is an excellent touch, especially with them not simply evaporating but <em>boiling</em>.</p>
<p>My only comment constructively comes from that journal in regards to bleeding water - I would think they'd catch on at some point earlier if they don't bleed, since someone is inevitably going to injure themselves and wonder where the hell the red stuff is.</p>
<p>In your first section discussing containment, you're using a Class Y &quot;mnestic&quot; - I think your word got guillotined.</p>

